<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nasjonal Samling</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1933–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nasjonal Samling was the Norwegian fascist party founded in 1933 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidkun-quisling">Vidkun Quisling</a>. It won little support at the polls, but when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> on 9 April 1940 Quisling tried to seize power. Under the German Reichskommissariat it became the only legal party and from 1942 formed a collaborationist government under Quisling. It was dissolved in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nasjonal-samling.jpg" alt="Nasjonal Samling" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ssolbergj · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nasjonal_Samling_insignia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
